Task 1:

repeat_purchase_flag:
This column represents the outcome we want to predict (whether a customer makes a repeat purchase within 30 days), so it is the target variable.

discount_used_on_repeat_order:
This column contains information that is only known after the repeat purchase happens, 
so including it would leak future information into the model and artificially inflate performance.


Task 2:

1. Data Preprocessing & Cleaning:

Before training any model, the data must be checked for missing values, incorrect formats, and outliers; otherwise, 
the model may learn from noisy or invalid data and produce unreliable predictions.

2. Train-Test Split (or Validation Strategy):

Splitting the data into training and testing sets ensures that the model is evaluated on unseen data, helping to measure real-world performance and avoid overfitting.
